/target
# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This workspace's members include
# `crates/gateway`, `crates/orchestrator`, `crates/vault`, `crates/kokoro` and the
# `torii` binary — the library convention of omitting the lockfile applies to crates
# whose consumers resolve their own versions, not to a workspace that ships binaries.
# Committing it is also what makes `cargo audit` possible (it audits a lockfile) and
# what lets CI pass `--locked` so a build pins what it resolved.
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
# Claude Code state/transcripts — can contain secrets. Never commit.
.claude/
# qlty: the project config (`.qlty/qlty.toml` + configs) IS committed so the
# scan is repo-controlled; `.qlty/.gitignore` already ignores the cache/output.
# Git worktrees for isolated feature work (superpowers workflow).
/.worktrees/
# Site design mockups — generated/exported artifacts, kept local, not tracked.
/docs/mockups/
